{"animath":"0.1","canvas":{"height":540,"width":960},"kind":"concept","level":"secondary","scenes":[{"caption":"Velocity is speed with a direction","duration_ms":9000,"id":"s1","narration":"An athlete sprints 100 metres in 20 seconds: her speed is distance over time — 100 divided by 20, which is 5 metres per second. Velocity adds direction: she ran right, so her velocity is 5 metres per second rightwards.","steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"title","kind":"text","size":34,"text":"Speed or velocity?","x":80,"y":70}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#2471a3","id":"formula","kind":"latex","size":40,"tex":"v = \\frac{d}{t}","x":80,"y":170}},{"at_ms":1000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"track","kind":"line","stroke":"#5d6d7e","width":4,"x1":120,"x2":840,"y1":320,"y2":320}},{"at_ms":1300,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"run0","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"0 m","x":100,"y":370}},{"at_ms":1500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"run100","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"100 m","x":820,"y":370}},{"at_ms":1700,"do":"show","shape":{"cx":120,"cy":320,"fill":"#f5cba7","id":"athlete","kind":"circle","r":20,"stroke":"#8e5a2b","width":2}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"move","dur_ms":2500,"target":"athlete","to":{"cx":840,"cy":320}},{"at_ms":5000,"do":"show","shape":{"color":"#1f7a3a","id":"work","kind":"latex","size":36,"tex":"v = \\frac{100\\ \\text{m}}{20\\ \\text{s}} = 5\\ \\text{m/s}","x":80,"y":450}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dir","kind":"text","size":24,"text":"direction: to the right  →  this is velocity","x":80,"y":510}},{"at_ms":7400,"do":"caption","text":"Velocity is speed with a direction attached."}]},{"caption":"Distance–time graphs: the gradient is the speed","duration_ms":10000,"id":"s2","narration":"On a distance–time graph, time runs along the bottom and distance up the side: this line climbs 120 metres in 60 seconds. A probe travels the line while the gradient triangle builds beneath it — gradient is rise over run: 120 over 60, which is 2 metres per second."